course: dictionary
lesson: 15634
title: Tenfold: ten times as much
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tenfold means ten times as much or as many. It is a useful word when something grows very fast. «The town's population grew tenfold in ten years.» That means the town became ten times bigger.
explain: Look for the clue in the numbers around it. «Mia had 2 stickers, and after swapping she has 20: a tenfold increase.» Two times ten is twenty, so tenfold means multiplied by ten.
explain: Tenfold can work as an adverb, as in «Sales grew tenfold», or as an adjective, as in «a tenfold increase». Try swapping in "ten times as much" to check your meaning. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Tenfold means ten times as much or as many.
fact: «Sales grew tenfold» means sales became ten times bigger.
fact: As an adjective, tenfold describes a noun, as in «a tenfold increase».
fact: Tenfold is often used in maths and science when you multiply by 10.
fact: A good check is to swap in "ten times as much" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Sales grew tenfold last month.» What does tenfold mean here? | *Ten times as much | Ten minutes later | Ten pounds exactly | Ten parts broken off
exercise: Ben's score went from 5 to 50. It was a ___ increase. Which word fits the gap? | slowly | *tenfold | halfway | quietly
exercise: «The rain was tenfold worse than yesterday.» What does tenfold suggest? | *Ten times worse | Slightly wetter | The same as yesterday | Ten minutes late
test: «The bakery needed tenfold more flour for the party.» What does tenfold mean? | *Ten times as much | Just a little more | Half as much | The same amount
test: Kai saved £2, and his savings grew tenfold. How much might he have now? | £200 | £2 | £12 | *£20
exam: Which sentence uses tenfold to mean ten times as many? | *The class grew tenfold, from 3 pupils to 30 pupils | The class grew tenderly around the teacher | The class grew slowly over the summer
